 Sequence Given Its Recursive Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25d55b98-960e-591e-bf2d-4f4a15f0caea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548429} {:answer/id #uuid "7c1a3798-54ab-540d-863e-f5e6a9544ee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548586} {:answer/id #uuid "9bdf55a5-f673-5863-95de-682e4913eded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548664} {:answer/id #uuid "a82bbcfe-69b8-5590-98b0-bca18d5ecc85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548686} {:answer/id #uuid "ec359335-db2b-5362-8e72-c6378e62b45f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bdf55a5-f673-5863-95de-682e4913eded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548664} :answer-field/id #uuid "41177c22-4ae0-5230-bc33-006cf9fb29c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "418f1354-66b6-535c-975e-7236a5d63898" :question/math-academy-id "q-79510" :question/problem "What is the $4$th term of the geometric sequence given below?\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=128,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the recursive formula to compute the terms of the sequence up to the $4$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =128 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{2}(128)=-64 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}(-64)=32 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{2}(32)=-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${a}_{4}=-16.$"}]}
